# Flask Website Screenshot Generator

A small Flask project that generates screenshots of websites using the ScreenshotBase API.

This project was built as a learning exercise while following the freeCodeCamp tutorial:

[Build a Website Screenshot Generator with Python and Flask](https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/build-a-website-screenshot-generator-with-python-and-flask/)

## What I learned

While building this project, I practiced:

- creating a Flask application
- handling `GET` and `POST` requests
- reading HTML form data with `request.form`
- making HTTP requests with the `requests` library
- using dictionaries for query parameters and headers
- working with environment variables using `os.getenv()`
- handling HTTP errors with `try` / `except`
- saving binary image data to a file
- rendering HTML templates with Flask

## Requirements

- Python
- Flask
- requests
- a ScreenshotBase API key

Install the dependencies with:

```bash
pip install flask requests
```

## Environment variable

Before running the application, set your ScreenshotBase API key:

```bash
export SCREENSHOTBASE_API_KEY="your_api_key"
```

## Run the application

```bash
python app.py
```

Then open:

```text
http://127.0.0.1:5000
```

in your browser.

## Project structure

```text
screenshot-generator/
├── app.py
├── static/
├── templates/
│   └── index.html
├── .gitignore
└── README.md
```

## Notes

The API key is not stored directly in the source code. It is loaded from the `SCREENSHOTBASE_API_KEY` environment variable.

The virtual environment and sensitive files should not be committed to GitHub.